## Summary

This draft PR brings the Fastify/Next.js Cartridge Store implementation forward with:

- versioned public API discovery and /api/v1 compatibility paths;
- firmware discovery and browser-based flashing workflow;
- standalone Fumadocs documentation service and updated repository documentation;
- Dream Platform/local development topology updates.

## Mandatory parity check

This PR is intentionally a **draft**. Before review or merge, we must compare the implementation against the legacy CartridgeStore branch and verify the complete Flask/Fastify parity surface, including:

- public Store and firmware routes;
- bundle validation and metadata/header handling;
- multiplayer behavior;
- USB flashing workflow;
- authentication, discovery, scores, metrics and compatibility aliases;
- deployment and environment contracts.

## Merge policy

**Do not enable automatic merge.** The target repository still contains legacy-branch history and the resulting divergence must be reviewed explicitly. This PR should be converted to ready-for-review only after the parity check is complete and any missing legacy behavior is addressed.

## Validation

The development stack was started with the Dream Platform overlay and verified through the configured .dream.test Store, docs and API health endpoints.

Fixes the valid [medium code-scanning alerts](https://github.com/Automattic/woocommerce-payments/security/code-scanning?query=is%3Aopen+severity%3Amedium).

#### Changes proposed in this Pull Request

The repository gives the default `GITHUB_TOKEN` write access. These 55 workflow alerts come from jobs that inherit it. Set read access for each workflow, then grant write access only to jobs that publish releases or docs, update the wiki, push release branches, or comment on PRs. The caller of the reusable release workflow also passes its required rights.

Two checkout paths handled error text as HTML. Sanitize classic checkout notices before adding them to the page, and parse Express Checkout notices in an inert document. This keeps the formatted WooCommerce notices and short Express Checkout messages intended in [#4436](https://github.com/Automattic/woocommerce-payments/pull/4436) and [#8937](https://github.com/Automattic/woocommerce-payments/pull/8937).

Alert [#59](https://github.com/Automattic/woocommerce-payments/security/code-scanning/59) concerns jQuery bundled with static REST API docs. I found no path from user input to its vulnerable HTML expansion, so this PR leaves that library unchanged. No public API or stored data changes. Multisite was not tested.

#### Testing instructions

**Classic checkout notice**

1. On a local test store, run `pnpm run watch`, add a product to the cart, and open the classic shortcode checkout with WooPayments selected. Paste this into the browser console:

   ```js
   const notice = `<ul class="woocommerce-error" role="alert"><li>Test error. <a href="#customer_details">Go to billing details</a><img src="x" onerror="console.error('unsafe handler ran')"></li></ul>`;
   for ( const config of [ window.wcpayConfig, window.wcpay_upe_config ] ) {
       if ( config ) {
           config.accountIdForIntentConfirmation = 'acct_test';
           config.genericErrorMessage = notice;
       }
   }
   window.Stripe = function () { throw new Error( 'Test checkout error' ); };
